Spec: Editor Module

Purpose:
  Canvas orchestration layer — connects tools, rendering, input, history,
  and snapping into a cohesive editing experience.

Structure:
  ./controller.ts: Central CanvasController class
  ./tool-manager.ts: Tool switching and delegation
  ./input.ts: Mouse, keyboard, wheel, pan input handling
  ./history.ts: Undo/redo stack with auto-save trigger
  ./snapping.ts: Snap point detection (endpoints, midpoints, grid, material)
  ./render/renderer.ts: Canvas 2D rendering (grid, shapes, selection, nodes, snap markers)
  ./Canvas.tsx: React component wrapping the HTML canvas

Owns:
  ./controller.ts
  ./tool-manager.ts
  ./input.ts
  ./history.ts
  ./snapping.ts
  ./render/**
  ./Canvas.tsx

Must:
  Render at most once per animation frame (rAF batching).
  Only trigger React re-renders when selectedIds actually change.
  Dispose all event listeners on unmount (no memory leaks).
  InputManager supports zoom-at-point via mouse wheel.
  SnapManager detects endpoints, midpoints, centers, material edges, and grid.
  History stack is limited to 50 entries.

Must not:
  Directly modify shape data — always delegate to commands.
  Re-render the canvas on every Zustand state change (only canvas-relevant changes).
  Use requestAnimationFrame polling loops (use on-demand rendering).

Depends on:
  @CanvasRenderer
  @ToolManager
  @InputManager
  @HistoryManager
  @SnapManager
  @useStore

Scenario: zoom with mouse wheel
  Given the canvas is at zoom level 1.0
  When the user scrolls the mouse wheel up (zoom in)
  Then the zoom level increases (e.g. to 1.25)
  And the zoom centers on the cursor position
  When the user scrolls down (zoom out)
  Then the zoom level decreases

Scenario: pan with middle mouse or space+drag
  Given the canvas is at pan (0, 0)
  When the user holds Space and drags the canvas
  Then the pan offset changes by the drag delta
  And shapes appear to move on screen

Scenario: undo via keyboard
  Given a shape has been created
  When the user presses Ctrl+Z
  Then the shape is removed (undo)
  When the user presses Ctrl+Shift+Z
  Then the shape is restored (redo)

Scenario: undo via toolbar buttons
  Given a shape has been created
  When the user clicks the Undo button in the toolbar
  Then the shape is removed
  When the user clicks the Redo button
  Then the shape is restored

Scenario: history stack limit
  Given the user has performed 60 actions
  Then the history stack retains only the last 50
  And undo cannot go back further than 50 steps

Scenario: snap to grid
  Given snapping is enabled and grid is visible
  When the user drags a shape near a grid intersection
  Then the shape snaps to the grid point
  And a snap indicator appears

Scenario: snap to endpoint
  Given snapping is enabled and shape A has a corner at (100, 100)
  When the user drags shape B's corner near (100, 100)
  Then it snaps to exactly (100, 100)
  And a snap marker is shown

Scenario: tool switching via keyboard shortcuts
  Given the Select tool is active
  When the user presses 'P'
  Then the Pen tool becomes active
  When the user presses 'V'
  Then the Select tool becomes active again

Scenario: canvas renders shapes correctly
  Given 3 shapes exist (rectangle, circle, path)
  When the canvas renders
  Then all 3 shapes are visible on the canvas
  And shapes on hidden layers are not rendered

Scenario: material boundary display
  Given material is set to 300x200mm
  Then a dashed rectangle representing the material boundary is visible
  And it measures 300x200mm in world coordinates
